TEXT 0 -544 Left 2 ;Project Task 1 - System D woofer (Scan-Speak 26W/8534G00) in its 88.1 L box, closed or vented. Driver and box values fitted to the Lab D impedances (box_model.py).
TEXT 0 -512 Left 2 ;IMPEDANCE analogy in all three domains: electrical V = voltage, I = current | mechanical V = force, I = velocity | acoustical V = pressure, I = volume velocity
TEXT 0 -464 Left 2 !.param Vg=1 Re=5.7 Le=0.001498 Bl=8.283 Mmd=0.03668 Rms=0.6085 Cms=0.0011735 Sd=0.034967 aD=0.1055 aP=0.0325
TEXT 0 -432 Left 2 !.param rho=1.2041 c=343.21 VB=0.088087 fill=1 CAB={VB*fill/(rho*c**2)}
TEXT 0 -400 Left 2 !.param MAP={table(cfg,0,1e+09,1,67.4382,2,82.9923,3,91.1884,4,52)}
TEXT 0 -368 Left 2 !.param RAP={table(cfg,0,1,1,348.944,2,387.098,3,405.763,4,306.411)}  RAL={table(cfg,0,1e+12,1,66113.8,2,66113.8,3,66113.8,4,66113.8)}
TEXT 0 -336 Left 2 !.step param cfg list 0 1 2 3 4
TEXT 0 -304 Left 2 ;cfg: 0 = plugged, 1 = L160, 2 = L200, 3 = L240, 4 = Mx   (vented: Q_L 5.2, Q_P 29.9 from the fit; plugged box fitted lossless.  cfg 4 = M_AP 52 kg/m^4, edit to explore)
TEXT 0 208 Left 2 ;acoustic load, in series: the box (C_AB || R_AL || vent M_AP + R_AP) between pD and pF, then the front radiation impedance Z_ar of the cone
TEXT 0 240 Left 2 ;V(pD,pF) = box pressure;  I(Vd3) = U_P, the vent volume velocity (outward);  far field ~ U_D - U_P
TEXT 0 1008 Left 2 !.param MA1=3.0837 RA1=5212.1 RA2=11819 CA1=4.9176e-08
TEXT 1664 144 Left 2 ;outputs (plot in dB): SPL = dB SPL at 1 m, half space; NFcone, NFvent = near-field pressure in Pa (dB re 1 Pa) for e_g = 1 V
TEXT 0 1040 Left 2 !.param kff={rho/(2*pi*20u)} knc={rho/(pi*aD)} knv={rho/(pi*aP)}
TEXT 0 1072 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 5 500
TEXT 0 1120 Left 2 ;SPL: p = j w rho (U_D - U_P) / (2 pi r), r = 1 m, half space (box on the floor / large baffle), no baffle step, no room.
TEXT 0 1152 Left 2 ;NF: p = j w rho U / (pi a) at the centre of a baffled piston, ka << 1 (Keele). Compare with Lab D labD_nf_*.mat, which are p/V in Pa/V.
